 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S445-009\", \"clauses\": {\"solve_area_problem\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"Ana has two rectangular flower beds: Bed 1 is {l1} {lu} by {w1} {lu} and Bed 2 is {l2} {lu} by {w2} {lu}. What is the combined total area of both flower beds in {unit_label}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 asks the learner to solve for an area (a combined total of two areas) from given side lengths. Its item (flower beds) is not in the F02 or F04 fault set, and its side ranges (2 to 10, with Bed 2 lengths 2 to 5 and widths 2 to 6) and sq m unit produce realistic whole-number areas.\"}, \"word_problem_context\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"Ana has two rectangular flower beds: Bed 1 is {l1} {lu} by {w1} {lu} and Bed 2 is {l2} {lu} by {w2} {lu}. What is the combined total area of both flower beds in {unit_label}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 is a word problem with a named person and a real-world setting; it is the family that produces problems in context without the F04 item/unit mismatch.\"}, \"extract_area_relationship_from_context\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F02\", \"template\": \"A rectangular {item_noun} has an area of {rect_area} {unit_label} and a {known_name} of {known_val} {lu}. What is its {other_name} in {lu}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F02 gives an area and one side in context and requires the learner to extract the area-length-width relationship to find the missing side. It is the family that best produces the extraction task, although it is itself listed as failing for item and unit realism.\"}, \"area_attribute\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"Ana has two rectangular flower beds: Bed 1 is {l1} {lu} by {w1} {lu} and Bed 2 is {l2} {lu} by {w2} {lu}. What is the combined total area of both flower beds in {unit_label}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The question asks for area in a square unit (sq m, printed through unit_label) of each bed and their total, so the attribute area is named and measured.\"}, \"square_figure\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"A square {item_noun} measures {s} {lu} on each side. What is its area in {unit_label}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F05 states a square by its side length (s, 2 to 5 m) and asks for its area, which addresses squares directly. Its item nouns are not in the F02 or F04 fault set.\"}, \"rectangle_figure\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"Ana has two rectangular flower beds: Bed 1 is {l1} {lu} by {w1} {lu} and Bed 2 is {l2} {lu} by {w2} {lu}. What is the combined total area of both flower beds in {unit_label}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 describes each figure as a rectangle with two different side lengths and asks for its area.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F02\", \"F04\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"A rectangular {item_noun} has an area of {rect_area} {unit_label} and a {known_name} of {known_val} {lu}. What is its {other_name} in {lu}?\", \"A rectangular {item_noun} is {l} {lu} long and {w} {lu} wide. What is the area of the {item_noun} in {unit_label}?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F04: the item_noun domain (one of the generator's own choices, members including bookmark, index card, rug, classroom floor, garden plot) is not coupled to the length domain, and lu is printed as both cm and m with side slots of 2 to 8. A bookmark or index card given as 8 m long, or a classroom floor given as 8 cm long, are both in the declared domains and are wrong statements about the world. F02: the item_noun domain includes card and photo, and the unit_label domain includes sq m with rect_area printed up to 40. A card with an area of 40 sq m is in the printed observations, which is a misleading context for a grade 3 learner. Its lu member is tied to the unit_label only by basis text, and the rect_area and known_val values are printed as independent slots. F05, F06 and the hint families were checked for the same item